-- title:
--   Uniqueness of a place over a simple root pair of Φₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let `data` be a modular-polynomial datum of level $p$: a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ that is monic in $Y$, whose degree in $Y$ equals $\psi(p)=\sum_{d \mid p,\ d \text{ squarefree}} p/d$, and which satisfies $\Phi(j(q), j(q^p)) = 0$ as a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, the substitution $X \mapsto j(q)$ being the ring homomorphism `evalAtJ`. Let $j_1, j_2$ be elements of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and assume that $\Phi$, specialised coefficientwise by $X \mapsto j_1$ and evaluated at $Y = j_2$, vanishes, and that $j_2$ is a root of multiplicity exactly $1$ of the one-variable polynomial $\Phi(j_1, Y) \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[Y]$. Let $F$ be `modularFunctionFieldBar p`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of the level-$p$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull p` $\subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and let $x, x'$ be places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from $F$ itself, and principal ideal rings; `ord` denotes the associated normalised $\mathbb{Z}$-valued valuation. Assume that at each of $x$ and $x'$ both $j(q) - j_1$ and $j(q^p) - j_2$ (that is, `jBar p` and `jpBar p` shifted by the images of $j_1$, $j_2$) have strictly positive order. Then $x = x'$.
--
--   This is the statement that at most one place of the function field of $X_0(p)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is centred at a point $(j_1, j_2)$ of the plane model $\Phi_p = 0$ at which $j_2$ is a simple root of $\Phi_p(j_1, Y)$, i.e. at which the model is smooth; at the nodes of the model, where $j_2$ is a multiple root, two places lie over the pair. It is the uniqueness companion of the corresponding existence statement and is used, together with the computation of the root multiplicity at a Vélu quotient, to single out the point of $X_0(p)$ attached to a pair consisting of an elliptic curve and a subgroup of order $p$, and in the local analysis at nodes of the model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_place_eq_of_modularPolynomial_rootMultiplicity_eq_one.lean

import Mathlib
